==============================================================================
[1] structure: det J, z-linearity, sign-diagonal equivariance group
==============================================================================
det J_F = -2  (expect -2; F is etale everywhere)
z-linear: F = A(x,y) z + B(x,y),  A = ((x*y + 1)**3, 3*x*(x*y + 1)**2, -x**3)  -- CONFIRMED
equivariances F(D p) = D' F(p):
   D=diag(1, 1, 1)  ->  D'=diag(1, 1, 1)
   D=diag(-1, -1, 1)  ->  D'=diag(1, -1, -1)
NOTE: sigma=diag(-1,-1,1) on the SOURCE pairs with tau=diag(1,-1,-1) on the
TARGET; sigma != tau, so the tower symmetry TWISTS.  A depth-2 symmetry needs
rho with F o rho = sigma o F; no sign-diagonal rho exists (list above), so no
sign-diagonal involution acts on the F o F fiber over v*: the naive 'sigma-
equivariant 1+2 iterate tree' prediction FAILS in its strong form.

